{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "class _PatternMapper:\n    \"\"\"Manages the one-to-one mapping between strings and pattern characters and detects inconsistencies.\n\n    Satisfies BR2, BR3, BR4.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._word_to_char_map: dict[str, str] = {}\n        self._char_to_word_map: dict[str, str] = {}\n\n    def establish_mapping(self, word: str, char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Attempts to establish or verify a mapping for a given word-char pair.\n\n        Returns True if the mapping is consistent, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Check consistency from word to char (BR3)\n        if word in self._word_to_char_map:\n            if self._word_to_char_map[word] != char:\n                return False # Word already mapped to a different char\n        # Check consistency from char to word (BR4)\n        if char in self._char_to_word_map:\n            if self._char_to_word_map[char] != word:\n                return False # Char already mapped to a different word\n\n        # If no existing conflicts, establish the mapping (BR2)\n        self._word_to_char_map[word] = char\n        self._char_to_word_map[char] = word\n        return True\ndef is_samepatterns(string_list: list[str], pattern_list: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a list of strings follows a given pattern.\n\n    Returns True if the sequence of strings follows the established pattern, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    # FR1, BR1: Validate input list lengths\n    if len(string_list) != len(pattern_list):\n        return False\n\n    mapper = _PatternMapper()\n\n    # FR2, BR2, BR3, BR4: Establish and verify consistent mapping\n    for i in range(len(string_list)):\n        word = string_list[i]\n        char = pattern_list[i]\n\n        if not mapper.establish_mapping(word, char):\n            return False # Inconsistency detected (BR6)\n\n    # FR3, BR5: All mappings consistent and sequence followed\n    return True"}
