{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "_memo = [1, 1]\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\"\"\"\n    if n <= len(_memo):\n        return _memo[n - 1]\n\n    # Calculate sequence terms from the current length of _memo up to n.\n    # The loop starts from the next term to compute (len(_memo) + 1).\n    for i in range(len(_memo) + 1, n + 1):\n        # P(i) = P(P(i-1)) + P(i-P(i-1))\n        # P(x) is stored at _memo[x-1]\n        p_i_minus_1_val = _memo[i - 2] # This is the value P(i-1)\n\n        term1 = _memo[p_i_minus_1_val - 1]\n        term2 = _memo[i - p_i_minus_1_val - 1]\n\n        p_i = term1 + term2\n        _memo.append(p_i)\n\n    return _memo[n - 1]"}
