{"task_id": "Mbpp/101", "solution": "def kth_element(array: list, k: int) -> any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the kth element in the given array using 1-based indexing.\n    Raises ValueError for invalid inputs (empty array, k out of bounds/non-positive).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input array cannot be empty.\")\n    if not isinstance(k, int) or k <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"k must be a positive integer.\")\n    if k > len(array):\n        raise ValueError(\"k is out of bounds for the given array.\")\n\n    # Convert 1-based index to 0-based index\n    zero_based_index = k - 1\n    return array[zero_based_index]"}
