{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def amicable_numbers_sum(upper_limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers from 1 to the specified upper limit.\n\n    Args:\n        upper_limit: The inclusive upper bound for the search.\n\n    Returns:\n        The total sum of unique amicable numbers found.\n    \"\"\"\n    def get_proper_divisor_sum(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given positive integer n.\"\"\"\n        if n <= 0:\n            return 0\n        if n == 1:\n            return 0\n\n        divisor_sum = 1\n        for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                divisor_sum += i\n                if i * i != n:\n                    divisor_sum += (n // i)\n        return divisor_sum\n\n    if upper_limit < 1:\n        return 0\n\n    amicable_sum = 0\n    found_amicable_numbers = set()\n\n    for a in range(1, upper_limit + 1):\n        if a in found_amicable_numbers:\n            continue\n\n        sum_div_a = get_proper_divisor_sum(a)\n\n        if sum_div_a == a:\n            continue\n\n        if sum_div_a > upper_limit or sum_div_a < 1:\n            continue\n\n        sum_div_b = get_proper_divisor_sum(sum_div_a)\n\n        if sum_div_b == a:\n            amicable_sum += a\n            amicable_sum += sum_div_a\n            found_amicable_numbers.add(a)\n            found_amicable_numbers.add(sum_div_a)\n\n    return amicable_sum"}
