{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def _find_first_occurrence(arr: list[int], n: int, x: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Helper function to find the index of the first occurrence of x in a sorted array arr.\n    Returns -1 if x is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\ndef _find_last_occurrence(arr: list[int], n: int, x: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Helper function to find the index of the last occurrence of x in a sorted array arr.\n    Returns -1 if x is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\ndef is_majority(sorted_array: list[int], n: int, target_element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(sorted_array, n, target_element)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(sorted_array, n, target_element)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    return count > (n / 2)"}
