{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "def larg_nnum(list, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list containing the n largest items from the input list.\n    Validates n to be non-negative and not exceeding list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n cannot be negative.\")\n    if n > len(list):\n        raise ValueError(\"n cannot exceed the length of the list.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Sort the list in descending order to easily pick the largest items.\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(list, reverse=True)\n\n    # Return the first n elements, which are the n largest.\n    return sorted_numbers[:n]"}
