{"task_id": "Mbpp/233", "solution": "def lateralsuface_cylinder(radius: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the lateral surface area of a cylinder using its radius and height.\n    It instantiates a Cylinder object to perform the calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    import math\n\n    class Cylinder:\n        \"\"\"Represents a cylinder and calculates its lateral surface area.\"\"\"\n\n        def __init__(self, radius: float, height: float):\n            # No validation as per constraints; assume valid input.\n            self._radius = float(radius)\n            self._height = float(height)\n            self._lateral_surface_area = 0.0\n\n        def calculate_lateral_surface_area(self) -> float:\n            \"\"\"Computes and returns the lateral surface area of the cylinder.\"\"\"\n            self._lateral_surface_area = 2 * math.pi * self._radius * self._height\n            return self._lateral_surface_area\n\n    cylinder = Cylinder(radius, height)\n    return cylinder.calculate_lateral_surface_area()"}
