{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(tuple_list: list[tuple]) -> dict[tuple, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the occurrences of unique canonical tuples in a list.\n    Each tuple is canonicalized by sorting its elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    from collections import Counter\n\n    def _canonicalize_tuple(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n        \"\"\"Converts a tuple into its canonical form by sorting its elements.\"\"\"\n        return tuple(sorted(input_tuple))\n\n    counts_map = Counter()\n    for original_tuple in tuple_list:\n        canonical_tuple = _canonicalize_tuple(original_tuple)\n        counts_map[canonical_tuple] += 1\n\n    return dict(counts_map)"}
