{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "def next_Perfect_Square(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the given number.\"\"\"\n    import math\n\n    # Calculate the square root of the number incremented by one.\n    # This step ensures that we are looking for a square strictly greater than 'number'.\n    temp_root = math.sqrt(number + 1)\n\n    # Determine the smallest integer greater than or equal to temp_root.\n    # This integer will be the root of the next perfect square.\n    next_root = math.ceil(temp_root)\n\n    # Square this next root to find the next perfect square.\n    return int(next_root * next_root)"}
