{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string using dynamic programming.\n    This function has O(N^2) time complexity, where N is the length of the input string.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_string)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of the substring input_string[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the dp table for lengths from 2 to n.\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if input_string[i] == input_string[j]:\n                if length == 2:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2\n                else:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # lis_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[i].\n    lis_sum = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sum[i] = max(lis_sum[i], lis_sum[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # lds_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at arr[i].\n    lds_sum = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sum[i] = max(lds_sum[i], lds_sum[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # The maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence is max(lis_sum[i] + lds_sum[i] - arr[i]).\n    # arr[i] is subtracted because it's counted twice (once in LIS and once in LDS) as the peak.\n    max_bitonic_sum = float('-inf')\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, lis_sum[i] + lds_sum[i] - arr[i])\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
