{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "from collections import Counter\ndef validate(integer: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks whether the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    This function uses a private helper to calculate digit frequencies.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _calculate_digit_frequency(number: int) -> dict[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the frequency of each digit in a given number, handling negative numbers by using their absolute value.\"\"\"\n        abs_number_str = str(abs(number))\n        return {int(digit): count for digit, count in Counter(abs_number_str).items()}\n\n    frequencies = _calculate_digit_frequency(integer)\n    for digit, freq in frequencies.items():\n        if freq > digit:\n            return False\n    return True"}
