{"task_id": "Mbpp/290", "solution": "def max_length(list_of_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sub-list with the maximum length in a list of lists.\n    Returns a tuple containing the maximum length and the corresponding sub-list, prioritizing the last encountered list in case of ties.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_len = 0\n    max_sub = []\n\n    for sub_list in list_of_lists:\n        current_len = len(sub_list)\n        if current_len >= max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            max_sub = sub_list\n            \n    return (max_len, max_sub)"}
