{"task_id": "Mbpp/427", "solution": "def change_date_format(date_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a date of yyyy-mm-dd format to dd-mm-yyyy format.\n    This function orchestrates the use of an internal Date class for conversion.\n    \"\"\"\n    class Date:\n        \"\"\"\n        Encapsulates date components (year, month, day) and provides methods\n        for parsing from 'yyyy-mm-dd' and formatting to 'dd-mm-yyyy'.\n        \"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, date_string: str):\n            self.parseYMD(date_string)\n\n        def parseYMD(self, date_string: str) -> None:\n            \"\"\"\n            Parses a date string in 'yyyy-mm-dd' format and sets internal\n            _year, _month, _day components.\n            \"\"\"\n            parts = date_string.split('-')\n            self._year = int(parts[0])\n            self._month = int(parts[1])\n            self._day = int(parts[2])\n\n        def convertToDMY(self) -> str:\n            \"\"\"\n            Returns the date formatted as 'dd-mm-yyyy'.\n            \"\"\"\n            return f\"{self._day:02d}-{self._month:02d}-{self._year}\"\n\n    date_obj = Date(date_string)\n    return date_obj.convertToDMY()"}
