{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "import math\ndef perfect_squares(lower_bound: int, upper_bound: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns all perfect squares within a given inclusive range.\n    Returns an empty list if no perfect squares are found or if the range is invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    if lower_bound > upper_bound:\n        return []\n\n    perfect_squares_list = []\n\n    # Perfect squares are non-negative. Adjust lower_bound if it's negative.\n    effective_lower_bound = max(0, lower_bound)\n\n    # Calculate the square roots of the bounds to determine the range of integers to check.\n    start_root = math.ceil(math.sqrt(effective_lower_bound))\n    end_root = math.floor(math.sqrt(upper_bound))\n\n    # Iterate through potential integer roots\n    for i in range(int(start_root), int(end_root) + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        # Check if the calculated square falls within the original inclusive range\n        if lower_bound <= square <= upper_bound:\n            perfect_squares_list.append(square)\n\n    return perfect_squares_list"}
