{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "def diff_even_odd(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the difference between the first even and first odd number found in the list.\"\"\"\n\n    def is_even(number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given number is even.\"\"\"\n        return number % 2 == 0\n\n    def is_odd(number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given number is odd.\"\"\"\n        return number % 2 != 0\n\n    def find_first_even(numbers_list: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the first even number in a list.\"\"\"\n        for num in numbers_list:\n            if is_even(num):\n                return num\n        # The design context implies that an even number will always be found for valid inputs.\n        # No explicit handling for not found case is required by the prompt's constraints.\n        return 0 # Placeholder for type consistency if no even number is found\n\n    def find_first_odd(numbers_list: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the first odd number in a list.\"\"\"\n        for num in numbers_list:\n            if is_odd(num):\n                return num\n        # The design context implies that an odd number will always be found for valid inputs.\n        # No explicit handling for not found case is required by the prompt's constraints.\n        return 0 # Placeholder for type consistency if no odd number is found\n\n    first_even = find_first_even(numbers)\n    first_odd = find_first_odd(numbers)\n    return first_even - first_odd"}
