{"task_id": "Mbpp/619", "solution": "def move_num(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Moves all numeric characters to the end of the given string,\n    preserving the relative order of both character types.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_numeric_chars = []\n    numeric_chars = []\n\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char.isdigit():\n            numeric_chars.append(char)\n        else:\n            non_numeric_chars.append(char)\n\n    return \"\".join(non_numeric_chars) + \"\".join(numeric_chars)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "def largest_subset(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the size of the largest subset from a list of numbers\n    where every pair (a, b) in the subset satisfies (a % b == 0 or b % a == 0).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    numbers.sort()\n    n = len(numbers)\n    dp = [1] * n\n    max_size = 1\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if numbers[i] % numbers[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], 1 + dp[j])\n        max_size = max(max_size, dp[i])\n\n    return max_size"}
