{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "def triangle_area(radius: float) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of the largest triangle that can be inscribed in a semicircle.\n    The largest triangle has its base along the diameter and its height equal to the radius, yielding area = radius^2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if radius < 0:\n        return None\n    return radius * radius"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[float], list2: list[float], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    The median of 2n elements is the average of the (n-1)-th and n-th elements (0-indexed) of the merged sorted list.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0\n    j = 0\n    m1 = -1\n    m2 = -1\n\n    for count in range(n + 1):\n        if i == n:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == n:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n\n    return (float(m1) + float(m2)) / 2.0"}
