{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "def check_smaller(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if each element of the second tuple is strictly smaller than its\n    corresponding element in the first tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Tuples must have the same number of elements.\")\n\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        # If at any point an element in tuple2 is not strictly smaller, return False.\n        if not (tuple2[i] < tuple1[i]):\n            return False\n\n    # If all elements passed the comparison, return True.\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/161", "solution": "from typing import List, Any, Set\ndef remove_elements(source_list: List[Any], elements_to_remove: List[Any]) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes all elements from source_list that are present in elements_to_remove.\n    Returns a new list containing elements from source_list not in elements_to_remove,\n    preserving their original relative order.\n    \"\"\"\n    elements_to_remove_set: Set[Any] = set(elements_to_remove)\n\n    result_list: List[Any] = []\n    for element in source_list:\n        if element not in elements_to_remove_set:\n            result_list.append(element)\n    return result_list"}
